  {
    "number": 105,
    "title": "Implement durable shared agent state and bounded provider emitters",
    "body": "Persist interpreted agent state through an exclusive host storage boundary so restarts and diagnostic cleanup preserve chosen labels and undismissed notices. The new `@jimmie-potts/agent-state` package provides deterministic reduction, immutable snapshots, independent bounded consumers, consumer-scoped acknowledgment, quiesced migration, and source provider emitters. Diagnostics retain only the newest 10,000 entries within 24 hours.\n\nRefs #3. OpenSpec `gh-3-agent-state-core` is synchronized and archived. The package consumes the frozen early #30 budgets and bundles the verified lifecycle 1.0 archive. Pixoo #31 owns the production host/storage adapter; #8 owns installed-provider qualification. No hooks, live state, clients or devices were changed.\n\nValidation on Node 24 and Python 3.14:\n\n- Build/type, controller contracts in both languages, lifecycle in both languages, MCP/service/protocol, all external package consumers, and both performance suites pass. The new state suite passes 74 Node tests and the shared 28-case Python snapshot corpus.\n- Workflow checks pass with six capabilities, 34 requirements, five archives and 15 workflow regression tests. Existing CI jobs and platform coverage are retained; the new checks run in the lifecycle matrix.\n- Guide generation, five maintenance tests, six-width browser/print checks and committed-output consistency pass. All nine Archify artifacts pass 9/9 validation; both changed viewers pass the four-size browser check. The lifecycle viewer's prior overflow was repaired. Guide source pins, shared-runtime text, migration explanation and #103 coverage were updated.\n- Repeated package builds produce identical bytes. The archive installs outside the checkout and passes imports, declarations, manifests, Node/process tests and Python fixtures. Current candidate archive SHA-256: `802404c9755cad662a9ac03c9e5eac112d1e354eb665e2f88e7aed3414dd41b4`.\n\nRemaining delivery gates: independent fixed-comparison Standards and Specification reviews, every configured current-head CI job, explicit approval of the current guide UI, guarded squash merge, merged-main CI, immutable release publication and issue/guide closeout. Public guide publication remains outside this source delivery. The served public guide still matches its older `950f7f6` edition.\n",
    "state": "open",
