  {
    "number": 104,
    "title": "docs: add BUNNY HTML design atlas and service references",
    "body": "BUNNY’s architecture and device interfaces are spread across separate repositories and planning records. This adds a linked HTML design atlas plus offline API and database references, with delivered source and future behavior marked separately.\n\n## Included\n\n- An overview, 26 component documents, a combined reading/print view and an explorable state/action diagram.\n- Three Scalar viewers and downloadable OpenAPI 3.1 documents covering 37 explicit Pixoo/Nanoleaf REST/SSE operations. Each operation links to its pinned source handler.\n- Three SchemaSpy reports covering 28 tables: Pixoo library, separate ownership lock and Nanoleaf state. They are generated from empty source-schema fixtures; no live database is opened. Declared foreign keys are shown without inferred relationships.\n- HTML refresh instructions, source/tool hashes, offline browser assets, generation checks and work-guide synchronization.\n\nThe planned BUNNY hub database remains conceptual. No product contract, service, hook, installation, device behavior or public deployment changes. Browser request controls are disabled because live testing must be integrated with the owning services’ origin and credential rules. The OpenAPI files use an inactive port-0 placeholder for native-client import.\n\n## Validation\n\n- All three OpenAPI files validate with Swagger Parser 13.0.0.\n- Three source-extraction tests pass; no application source is executed by the DDL extractor.\n- Static checks pass for 28 reading pages and 53 reference pages, 37 operations, 28 table definitions, source pins, local references and bundled asset receipts.\n- Browser checks pass for Scalar search, every operation/table, desktop/mobile layout, navigation, themes, print, offline assets and no page errors. No service or device requests are made.\n- Two single-threaded SchemaSpy rebuilds produce identical file receipts.\n- Node 24 workflow validation passes for four specifications and four archived changes; all 15 workflow tests pass. Guide build, five maintenance tests and browser checks pass.\n\nSource pins: Hub `514b566279f271451e36a5bb86b166bfa2a33bd8`, Pixoo `9f1c0ec75651810a441606b0c08fbdeee824c8d8`, Nanoleaf `2558df5a2fc543247b0c75898ef0260ba3ea264b`.\n\n## Remaining delivery gates\n\nCandidate: `0a029966f82fe31958616be3241fb2e9b76c89de`; comparison base and merge-base: `514b566279f271451e36a5bb86b166bfa2a33bd8`.\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews report no findings on this fixed candidate. Both verified all 31 source-file hashes; Standards also reran the complete offline reference browser checks. Explicit human approval of this HTML candidate is pending.\n\nAll 13 current-head GitHub jobs failed before starting because GitHub reports failed account payments or a spending-limit restriction. Resolve the account restriction and rerun both workflows; every configured job must pass before an eligible guarded merge. Local verification does not replace this gate.\n\nThe repository-owned work guide is synchronized. Public publication remains outside scope; the public copy has not changed. No installation, real-client or physical acceptance is claimed.\n\nCloses #103\n",
    "state": "open",
